<title>HUNGARY: Hungary five-yr govt-bond yield set at 15.69 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary five-yr govt-bond yield set at 15.69 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the first issue of Hungary's five-year government bonds was set by auction at 15.69 percent, the Government Debt Management Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    BONDS OF THE 2001/C SERIES   HTBK</p>
<p>    Date of issue		 3 February 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 December 2001</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     30,732.86 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 6,000 million forints @</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	  15.69 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		   99.63 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - It was the first time ever that Hungary sold five-year government bonds. The 2001/C bond bears an annual interest of 15 percent, to be paid twice annually starting with June 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
